Afterglow: licence scope

The MIT licence below covers the source code of this repository (code, scripts, documentation and the data files
the code generates and reads), except the parts listed here.

NOT covered by the MIT licence: (c) 2026 Leonxlnx, all rights reserved. A listed file is excluded as a whole,
including any code in it. These parts are visible here for study: you may read them and rebuild the film and the
soundtrack locally for your own study, but no other right is granted (no copying, publishing, performing,
recording or arranging of the music, and no redistribution of the film, the audio or the stills).

1. The musical composition "Afterglow" and every file that encodes its notes:
     music/afterglow_melody.py                  the tune, note by note
     music/afterglow_arr.py                     both hands' accompaniment, harmony timeline, pedal plan
     music/afterglow_score.py                   form, tempo map, dynamics and voice levels; assembles the score
     sandbox/music-research/sketch.py           the composition sketch (chord chart, form, melody, left-hand
                                                patterns, tempo map) with the score checks afterglow_score.py uses
     research/music.md                          the composition brief: the chorus hook note by note, the chord
                                                charts with their voicings, the left-hand patterns
     music/final/                               every file: score.json, score.mid, leadsheet.txt, checks.txt,
                                                report.txt, roll_01_intro.png ... roll_13_coda.png, roll_full.png
     music/candidates/arranger/score.py         earlier versions of the piece:
     music/candidates/groove/score.py, sec_a.py, sec_b.py, sec_c.py, sec_d.py
     music/candidates/melody/score.py, melodies.py, chords.py, arr.py
     music/candidates/arranger/, groove/, melody/: score.json, score.mid, leadsheet.txt, checks.txt, report.txt,
                                                roll_*.png
     the performance tracks (release asset afterglow_perf_g1f.zip: perf.json, perf.bin, qc.json), whose key, hammer
     and damper tracks encode the notes
2. The film and its renders: the film (afterglow_1080p60.mp4), the audio renders of the composition (the
   soundtrack afterglow.wav and afterglow.mp3), and the stills in docs/stills/.

Third-party assets keep their own licences, as listed in docs/CREDITS.md (among them the Detmold impulse
response in music/ir/, CC BY 4.0, the MakeHuman / MPFB parts of the pianist asset, CC0 1.0, and the meshoptimizer
decoder, MIT).

